## Files You Should Not Edit Casually

<!-- List this repo's protected files and why. Standard categories: -->

- **Generated files** — <!-- name the regeneration command instead of hand-editing -->
- **Vendored / third-party code** — re-generate or update upstream, do not refactor in place.
- **Submodules** — read-only; changes go through the upstream repo.
- **Applied migrations** — never edit a committed migration; add a new one.
- **Lockfiles** — mutate only via the package manager; never add a second lockfile for a different package manager.
- **Shared test doubles / fixtures** — changing them changes every consumer.

